The cell 'span verbatim in the document / value absent from the span' specifies that the span is exactly present in the document and the value is not contained within that span. For the kernel `conformance.kernel.grounding`, the rule states it provides the grounding verdict with "no relaxation, value-in-span checked" [4756991799bcd6c4]. In the input, the span "The sky is blue" is verbatim in the document and the value "red" is absent from the span; the rule implies a verdict of VALUE_NOT_IN_SPAN. In the rewritten text, I change the value to "blue", which is now a substring of the span. The rule then implies a verdict of GROUNDED. Thus, the verdict moves.
